From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 15:51:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] thunderbolt: qcom: Add Glymur USB4 router MCU and firmware
 helpers

The USB4 host router of Qualcomm Glymur SoCs has a microcontroller (MCU)
that runs firmware loaded by the host. The host uploads the firmware
image and a router DROM into MCU RAM, starts the MCU and then passes
Type-C link changes to it through a command mailbox. The MCU reports
events through a ring in its shared memory.

Add helpers for these steps, without platform ownership of power,
clocks or resets:
- firmware image validation and upload (records of offset, word count
  and words, validated as a whole before the first write);
- the router DROM, with a UID derived from the SoC serial number;
- MCU layout setup for the legacy and v2 register layouts, upload, DROM
  write, start with its ready handshake, stop and mailbox commands;
- the MCU event ring decoder;
- encoders for the Type-C connect (USB4 and TBT3), preset and disconnect
  mailbox commands, from the enter_usb_data and typec_thunderbolt_data
  that the Type-C mux receives.

The register layout, firmware image format, upload and start handshake,
DROM contents, event ring format and command encodings match what the
platform's Windows driver uses on the Surface Laptop 8. The helpers are
built with the host router driver, which adds the Kconfig entry.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
